        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leff Pouishnoff, Frédéric Chopin, Franz Schubert, Robert Schumann, Franz Liszt\n- Works: Symphony No. 6 in C major, D. 589\n- Topics: Piano performance, Classical composition\n\nFacts:\n- Franz Schubert was an Austrian composer who lived from 31 January 1797 to 19 November 1828.\n- Franz Schubert composed the Symphony No. 6 in C major, D. 589, between October 1817 and February 1818.\n- Leff Pouishnoff was especially associated with performances of works by Frédéric Chopin.\n- Leff Pouishnoff also performed works by Franz Schubert, Robert Schumann, and Franz Liszt.",
